WEBVTT

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:48.080
A Tear-colored Rondo.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:03.960
Lili, come out, please.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.850
Kahoko Hino.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:13.370
I'm not sure I can face you.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:19.360
The magical violin I gave to you caused you much pain and suffering.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:25.070
It's fine now. Anyway, I've come to return this.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:27.370
I can't play it anymore, after all.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:32.490
Kahoko Hino, are you sure that this is it?

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.760
Yes, please.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:35.890
Do you understand?

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:39.720
I see. I understand.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:45.210
I'm grateful for all you've done so far to satisfy my selfish wish.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.170
Farewell.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.250
You love the violin, don't you?

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.360
I...

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:04.040
Aren't those tears what you are really feeling?

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:14.310
I'm not your food!

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:32.750
Kaho-sempai?

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.570
So you've started practicing again?

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:42.530
No. I won't play the violin anymore.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.480
Kaho-sempai, please don't say that.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:51.430
I love your violin playing.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:53.920
But my violin playing is...

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:58.070
When I listen to it, I feel my confidence building up!

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.670
My violin playing is not something so grand.

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:06.140
Fuyuumi-chan, please do your best for the final selection.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.190
I'll be rooting for you.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.350
Sempai.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.280
Kaho-sempai.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.500
Kaho-chan, good morning.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:18.970
Good morning, Kaho.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:19.940
Good morning.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.020
Kaho-chan, your violin...

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.170
Are you going to start practicing again?

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:29.770
No, I was thinking of parting with it.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.840
And withdrawing from the competition.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.790
Withdraw? Are you sure about that?

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:40.380
It was impossible for me from the start.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:43.260
But I think it's impossible for you to go back now.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:49.270
What are you saying? I'll just go back to the way I was before the competition.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:51.140
But we can't go back.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:57.230
Now that we love the Kaho who plays violin, we can't go back to the past.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:04.810
And so now it's time for the final selection.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:12.120
Everyone probably knows already, but Yunoki is going to study in England, so he withdrew.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.870
Um, what about Kaho-sempai?

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:21.250
Kaho-sempai said she was quitting the violin.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:27.090
She might withdraw as well...

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:47.550
I only came this far because Kaho-sempai was here with me.

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:55.310
Kanayan.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.310
Why didn't you stop her?

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:02.710
Why didn't you stop Kaho-chan?

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:11.350
You shouldn't be worrying about others. Your performance at the third selection wasn't like you.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:23.030
This is the final one. I hope you'll let me hear one of your fresh performances, just like you always do.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.270
See you.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:32.160
Bye, bye.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:35.120
Shimizu-kun?

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:38.950
You have some business with Kaho-chan, maybe?

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:40.170
Yes.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.880
Kaho already went home today.

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:48.360
Shimizu-kun.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:58.230
I see. So Hino-san might withdraw.

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:00.190
It's really quite shocking.

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:04.400
What should I do now?

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:08.600
All we can do now is watch over her.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:19.920
Why is everyone trying to get me to play the violin?

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:23.920
Even though I have no right to play the violin.

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:32.210
I don't want to deceive everyone anymore.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:33.810
Hino-sempai.

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:38.770
Shimizu-kun?

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:11.280
Just like the score.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:17.830
Each note, one after another, accurately...

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:22.560
That's the way I was to obtain the ideal sound.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:30.860
But if I imagine Hino-sempai's sound...

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:37.530
A sound is born that resonates in a way it never has before.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:52.000
How... incredibly pleasant.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:56.730
Could this be, perhaps...

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:07.740
Please let me hear it.

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:10.980
Let me hear your sound, Sempai.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:18.120
When I hear you play, Sempai...

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:23.050
I feel like I may be able to grab hold of it.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:27.380
Grab hold of something very important.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:30.380
My sound...

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.680
Please.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:37.860
I need your sound, Sempai.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.580
But my sound is a fake.

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:44.720
I feel my confidence building up!

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:46.880
It's because you were there that I...

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:50.030
You love playing the violin, don't you?

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:52.190
I'm sorry.

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:57.110
I don't have any right for you to say something like that to me.

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:00.400
I apologize.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:04.780
I'm not going to play the violin anymore.

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:19.020
Kaho-sempai...

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.140
Be careful on your way home!

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:28.670
Hino-san!

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.180
Hey, going home right now?

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:33.100
Yes.

00:10:42.020 --> 00:10:43.880
Want to hang out with me for a bit?

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:59.080
Are you scared of heights?

00:10:59.080 --> 00:10:59.970
No...

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.410
Oh, thank goodness.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:07.140
I like to go up to high places like this and look out on the city.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:10.280
It makes you realize how small your existence really is.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:17.360
But for me, it also makes me realize just how big the world is, and that makes me excited.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:20.610
Excited?

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:26.240
Yeah! In this vast world there are countless people.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:31.000
And when I think of the music that those countless numbers create,

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.550
it just sounds really fun.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:41.700
This time I'm having the students in the violin class have a volunteer concert.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.260
With those children?

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:45.510
Everyone is trying really hard.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:52.900
When I see that, I think that music really isn't something special, you know?

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:55.760
Not something special?

00:11:55.760 --> 00:12:01.740
I think the threshold is especially high for classical music, and it's thought of as something quite refined.

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:07.490
But it's really no different than normal talking, or laughing, or playing around, you know?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:16.040
You look like you're worried about something, but you shouldn't force yourself to make a decision.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:20.700
And during that time, an answer will come to you naturally.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:22.800
Osaki-sempai...

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:53.920
My answer. Yes, I love the violin.

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:56.540
I want to play the violin.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:03.480
But playing a violin without any magic... Is something I cannot do.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:07.350
I'm sorry, Osaki-sempai.

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:12.060
I'm afraid to face my own feelings.

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:30.870
I'm sorry. Shimizu-kun?

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:35.660
Tsukimori-sempai...

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:39.060
I'm sorry.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:40.250
Don't worry about it.

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:45.510
Oh, no.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:52.960
Here.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.650
Thank you very much.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.140
Tsukimori-sempai?

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:03.070
What is it?

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:08.490
Have you made a woman cry before?

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:17.320
I wonder why she started crying?

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:19.970
Kaho-sempai...

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:23.170
Kaho? Hino was...

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:32.040
What in the world could be causing her such pain?

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:37.800
Hihara?

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:44.270
What's the matter? You seem really absent-minded lately.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:49.990
Why did you start playing the flute, Yunoki?

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:53.450
Well...

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:59.100
It's sort of a difficult thing for me to answer.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:00.910
Is there something the matter?

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:02.110
No.

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.210
I was just curious, that's all.

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.430
I see.

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:08.820
But, I'm a bit relieved.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:13.140
Even you have things you can't answer.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:19.510
Well, that's because I'm human, too.

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:21.090
See you.

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:34.490
I started the flute because my brothers played the piano.

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:42.460
So that no matter what, I would never surpass my brothers at something.

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:48.690
It's more difficult to deceive yourself than it is to deceive others, huh?

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:05.570
I withdraw.

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:09.530
I don't want to anymore. That's what I've decided.

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:14.010
How can you quit so easily?

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:21.910
That day, the first time I was in a piano competition...

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:25.960
I fell into despair when it came to music.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:29.760
And ever since then I stopped performing in front of other people,

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:32.190
entered the soccer team at school,

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:35.250
and continued to play the piano at home.

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:38.400
I couldn't stop completely.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:41.060
But I also couldn't play honestly.

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:45.730
I have no need for people who can't decide and do everything halfway.

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:51.540
I really do only do things halfway, don't I?

00:16:56.230 --> 00:16:57.470
Hino?

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:06.180
No...

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:32.360
Ave Maria?

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:36.530
It sounded better that time at the retreat.

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:05.070
Why did I say something like that?

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:15.360
But it's true, that was surely some amazing playing back then.

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:18.560
That Ave Maria...

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:42.710
I'm sorry, Lili. I'm just going to leave this here quietly.

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:49.770
This time, I'm really going to...

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:56.990
Goodbye.

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:15.150
I can't! If I turn around now, I'll...

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.850
It's Ave Maria.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:15.850
Ever since I met this magical violin, so many wonder things have happened.

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:23.200
And thanks to that violin, I met all of you... And yet!

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:30.960
And during that time, an answer will come to you naturally.

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:34.580
In the end, I just don't want to leave you!

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:44.910
I'm sorry! I made you go through such a horrible ordeal...

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:48.890
But even so, I want to play you!

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:52.170
Will you forgive me?

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:54.340
Wouldn't it be nice to play again?

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:56.530
Of course!

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:04.470
Lili...

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:08.140
Kahoko Hino, I am truly glad.

00:21:08.690 --> 00:21:13.670
I'm just so glad that this violin didn't make you hate music...

00:21:14.630 --> 00:21:15.760
So glad...

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:16.920
Lili...

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:20.750
If you fix the broken strings you can play it again.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:23.200
There's no magic power left.

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:24.830
Are you still OK with that?

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:29.430
Yeah. I want to play this violin!

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:31.090
I see.

00:21:31.090 --> 00:21:37.500
Even if the strings break, the bond between you and this violin will never break.

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:38.750
Bond?

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:41.360
Didn't you know, Kahoko Hino?

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:45.000
String is "corda" in Italian.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:49.120
And corda also means "bond."

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:03.980
Corda... Bond...

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:39.730
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:40.620 --> 00:23:45.060
The clarinet, a wind instrument, was invented in the 18th century.

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:48.800
It's pretty recent compared to other classical instruments.

00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:52.240
It's a type of instrument that produces a sound by breathing through

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:56.250
a thin piece of wood called a reed attached to the mouthpiece to make it vibrate.

00:23:56.250 --> 00:23:58.010
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:58.010 --> 00:24:05.030
You remember the nursery rhyme called "My Clarinet Broke," right? What country did the melody come from?

00:23:58.010 --> 00:24:05.040
"My Clarinet Broke" (Kurarinetto Kowashichatta) is an original Japanese nursery rhyme.

00:24:05.520 --> 00:24:08.630
Everyone, I'm sorry for worrying you!

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:11.430
Kahoko Hino is back, starting today!

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:14.680
I'm not going to let anyone do the preview for me anymore!

00:24:15.170 --> 00:24:18.310
Next episode: Once More, Andante.

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:20.060
Wait, isn't it al dente?

00:24:20.320 --> 00:24:23.630
The answer is... France!
